      "layout": "raw",
      "id": "vocab-reciprocal",
      "step": 1,
      "background_color": "#1a1a2e",
      "body": "<style>.rv{border-collapse:collapse;margin:15px auto;max-width:760px;width:100%}.rv td{color:#fff;font-size:36px;padding:10px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12);text-align:left}</style><h2 style=\"color:#fff;text-align:center;font-size:47px;margin-bottom:12px\">Reciprocal verbs</h2><table class=\"rv\"><tr><td>teach yourself</td><td>blame yourself</td></tr><tr><td>introduce myself</td><td>hurt yourself</td></tr><tr><td>amuse themselves</td><td>convince himself</td></tr><tr><td>prepare ourselves</td><td>help yourselves</td></tr></table>",
      "notes": "New grammar before Exercise 3. The verb goes with the right reflexive pronoun: myself, yourself, himself, herself, ourselves, yourselves, themselves. Quick example: I taught myself to swim."
    },
